summary:
  The answer of a play command that was replaced counts for the newer one.

history:
  A listener who switches stations quickly sends a device two play
  commands, and the first one's refusal can come home before the second
  has answered. Believed, it would end a cast that is about to succeed and
  blame the device for a station nobody listens to any more. An answer
  counts only for the command the device is still waited on for, by the
  number that command carries.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      if (typeof uuid !== "string" || uuid === "" || s.pending[uuid] !== seq)

replace:
      if (typeof uuid !== "string" || uuid === "" || s.pending[uuid] === undefined)

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_a_late_answer_of_an_older_attempt_changes_nothing.
  Line-neutral.
